    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.34.1</title>
      <pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:00:40 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>23401</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.34.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><p><strong>Tabs stay put; the Room reads like a room.</strong></p><ul><li>Each pond keeps exactly the tabs you opened, in your order, across restarts. A new pond opens on its Dashboard with no tabs, and Squeak never adds tabs by itself. Closing a duck's tab no longer puts it off duty.</li><li>"Delete Duck…" in a duck's menu removes it for good. Off duty and Bring back are there too.</li><li>Ducks have short names, and lines between ducks say who they went to.</li><li>A duck's run of status lines folds into one row; tap "+N earlier" to see the rest. Off duty ducks are listed in their own group in the roster.</li><li>The @ and / suggestion lists open above the composer instead of running off the bottom.</li><li>Ducks stay on duty when Squeak restarts; they go off duty only after an idle hour.</li><li>When a duck shows you a file, it opens in the app and the Artifacts list updates.</li><li>A duckling shows the model it really runs on, the same in its timeline row and in the helper strip.</li><li>Try the new layout in Settings › General (off by default): a row of your ducks instead of tabs, the Pond panel beside the Room, and each duck's Changes, Files, Canvas and Terminal in a pane beside its chat.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.34.0</h4><p><strong>The Room works for you.</strong></p><ul><li>Say "make it a task" in a pond's Room and Squeak gives it to the best duck: one already on related work, or a new duck. It starts at once; turn on "Ask before starting" in Pond settings if you'd rather tap Go.</li><li>Ducks post one short line when they take a task, get stuck, hand off or finish. Tap a line to read more. Bigger tasks get a plan card you can comment on.</li><li>@mention a duck to give it work directly. Ducks hand work to each other the same way, in the Room where you can see it.</li><li>Each pond has a shared Notebook of lessons its ducks have learned, readable and editable in Pond settings.</li><li>Ducks go off duty after an idle hour and come back when related work arrives. Pond settings set how many ducks work at once (4 by default).</li><li>In folder ponds, two ducks can't edit the same file at once; they sort it out in the Room.</li><li>"Make it a Git Pond…" in a pond's ⋯ menu puts a folder pond on GitHub (private by default). "Invite someone…" is there too.</li><li>Members of a shared pond can follow the Room and post in it; their tasks wait for your approval unless you give them Collaborator.</li><li>Tidier window: the layout picker moved to Window › Workspace, duplicate buttons are gone, tabs drop before or after by half, ⌃⇧← and ⌃⇧→ move a tab, and canvas Fit eases instead of jumping.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.33.3</h4><p><strong>Quitting is quitting.</strong></p><ul><li>When macOS or a script asks Squeak to quit (a kill signal), it now quits normally instead of being cut off, so it no longer reports a false "closed unexpectedly" next time.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
